2026-10-06 11:08:22 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-06 11:08:22 [deepseek-flash] • Fixed:* `distill` is now awaited at the call site. The unawaited-write race is gone,
2026-10-06 11:08:22 [deepseek-flash] though only because the write is commented out.
2026-10-06 11:08:22 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-10-06 11:08:22 [deepseek-flash] • New bug, and it is the important one:* the loop enumerates `history/` but reads `raw/` +
2026-10-06 11:08:22 [deepseek-flash] `file.name`. So the refined output is never read. The pipeline is raw → refine → history → distill,
2026-10-06 11:08:22 [deepseek-flash] but distill is re-reading raw and ignoring what refine produced. Either that is intentional
2026-10-06 11:08:22 [deepseek-flash] (distill is meant to be an independent pass over raw with a different filter) or the read path
2026-10-06 11:08:22 [deepseek-flash] should be `history/`. Given the file comment says "for all files in history/", it looks like a
2026-10-06 11:08:22 [deepseek-flash] leftover.
