2026-10-23 09:45:13 [simon@midnightblue.local] how do i enable chain of thought logging in claude api?
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 claude-haiku-5-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.003 768B 6.55s
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] You can get Claude's reasoning by turning on extended thinking in your Messages API
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] request. Set the `thinking` parameter to enabled and give it a `budget_tokens` value, which caps
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] how many tokens Claude can spend thinking. The budget must be at least 1,024 and less than
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] `max_tokens`.
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] The response then includes content blocks of type `thinking`, which contain the reasoning text,
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] alongside the usual `text` blocks with the final answer. To log the chain of thought, capture the
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] `thinking` blocks from the response and store them with the request ID and final answer. If you
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] stream the response, the reasoning arrives as `thinking_delta` events that you can accumulate.
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] A few things to keep in mind:
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] - Redacted blocks: Some thinking may come back as `redacted_thinking` blocks, which contain
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] encrypted content you can't read. Your logging should handle them without failing.
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] - Summaries: On newer Claude 4 models, the returned thinking may be a summary of the full
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] reasoning, while you are still billed for the full thinking tokens. Check the current docs for your
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] model.
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] - Multi-turn and tool use: If you send the conversation back, include the thinking blocks
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] unchanged, especially when tool use is involved.
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] - Sensitive data: Reasoning can echo user input or sensitive content, so apply the same
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] retention and access controls you use for other logs.
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] Parameter names and supported options change between model versions, so check Anthropic's extended
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] thinking documentation for the model you're using.
2026-10-23 09:45:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
