2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] Yes. When extended thinking is enabled, the thinking appears in `content` as separate content
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] blocks, not as a separate field.
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] `content` is a list of blocks, and each block has a `type`:
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] - `thinking` blocks contain the model's reasoning in a `thinking` field, along with a
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] `signature`.
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] - `redacted_thinking` blocks appear in place of `thinking` blocks when some reasoning is
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] encrypted for safety reasons.
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] - `text` blocks contain the visible answer.
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] The thinking blocks usually come before the text blocks. So if you read the first block's text
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] without checking its type, you may get the reasoning instead of the answer. Filter for blocks with
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] `type == "text"` to get the reply.
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] If you're using tool use with extended thinking, pass the thinking blocks back unchanged in the
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] next request, since the API needs them to continue the conversation correctly.
2026-10-23 10:54:20 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
