2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 claude-haiku-5-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.001 2.584KB 2.90s
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] Yes. With the Anthropic Messages API, when extended thinking is enabled, the response `content` is
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] an array of blocks, and the thinking appears as its own block(s) alongside the text. The thinking
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] blocks have `type: "thinking"` and carry a `thinking` field with the reasoning text, plus a
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] `signature` field. If the model's reasoning is redacted, you may instead see `type:
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] "redacted_thinking"` with an encrypted `data` field. The final answer is in one or more `type:
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] "text"` blocks.
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] So `reply.content` will not be a single text string. If you read it as one, you may pick up the
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] thinking, or get nothing useful, depending on block order. A safe pattern is to filter by type:
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] text_parts = [block.text for block in reply.content if block.type == "text"]
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] answer = "".join(text_parts)
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] Some SDK versions also offer a convenience property, but filtering by `type` is the most reliable
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] way to check what your harness is receiving. Also, when you pass the conversation back in a later
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] turn with tool use or thinking, you generally need to send the thinking blocks back unmodified,
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] including their signatures, so it's worth preserving the full `content` list in your history.
2026-10-23 11:52:17 [claude-haiku-5-5] 
