2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] Here are several terms for people who enjoy annoying others for fun, depending on the context and
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] tone:
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] 
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] • Online and Gaming*
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] • Troll: The most common modern term for someone who intentionally upsets, provokes, or
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] annoys people online for their own amusement.
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] • Griefer: Specifically used in multiplayer gaming for someone who deliberately irritates
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] and harasses other players (e.g., destroying their work or blocking their progress) just to ruin
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] their experience.
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] 
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] • General and Formal*
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] • Provocateur: Someone who deliberately behaves controversially in order to provoke an
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] argument or strong reaction.
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] • Agitator or Instigator: Someone who stirs up trouble or conflict just to watch
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] the fallout.
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] • Antagonist: A person who actively opposes or is hostile to someone, often just to get a
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] rise out of them.
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] 
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] • Lighthearted or Playful*
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] • Wind-up merchant (British slang): Someone who loves teasing or fooling others just to see
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] them get flustered.
2026-10-31 11:35:09 [gemini-4-argon] • Button-pusher: Someone who knows exactly what irritates a specific person and
